      "id": "CVE-2026-14613",
      "publishedDate": "2026-07-03T15:16:44.640Z",
      "lastModifiedDate": "2026-07-03T15:16:44.640Z",
      "description": "A vulnerability was discovered in Keycloak's administrative interface that allows certain administrators to see information about groups they shouldn't have access to. When the new Fine-Grained Admin Permissions (FGAP v2) are turned on, an administrator who is allowed to see a specific \"role\" can also see a list of all groups assigned to that role. The system fails to check if the administrator has permission to see those specific groups. This could allow a restricted administrator to discover \"hidden\" groups and see their details, such as internal names and custom settings, which might contain sensitive deployment information.",
      "severity": 4.3,
